# "Hello ULP", the milestone 3 demo, interactive: Ocean Blue (an operator)
# and Cymbal Shoes (a shipper) on localhost. You book, watch the voyage's
# events arrive signed and verified, then disrupt it and watch the alert.
#
#   dev/demo/hello-ulp [--tmux] [DIR]
#
# Builds the binaries and writes keys and configs into DIR (default
# $TMPDIR/supercargo-demo; keys are kept between runs), then prints the
# command for each of four terminals, or opens them in a tmux session with
# --tmux. dev/smoke/push runs the same demo, scripted.
#
# Environment: OP_PORT (8441), SH_PORT (8442), HOURS_PER_SECOND (1: the
# voyage departs about half a minute after booking and arrives about two
# and a half minutes later), ULP_LLM (fake: deterministic answers, no key;
# anthropic: Ocean Blue answers inquiries and Cymbal summarizes alerts with
# Claude, the key from ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in both nodes' terminals),
# ULP_OTEL_ENDPOINT (export both nodes' traces to this OTLP/HTTP collector,
# e.g. localhost:4318 after dev/demo/otel up), HELLO_ULP_SESSION (the
# tmux session name, hello-ulp; give tests their own so they never replace
# a running demo).
#
# In tmux, mouse mode is on for this session: click a pane to switch to it,
# use the wheel to scroll, drag a border to resize.
set -euo pipefail
. "$(dirname "$0")/../smoke/lib.sh"

tmux=false
if [[ "${1:-}" == "--tmux" ]]; then
  tmux=true
  shift
fi
dir="${1:-${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/supercargo-demo}"
mkdir -p "$dir"
dir="$(cd "$dir" && pwd)"

OP_PORT="${OP_PORT:-8441}"
SH_PORT="${SH_PORT:-8442}"
hps="${HOURS_PER_SECOND:-1}"

echo "Building ulpnode, ulpctl and ulpchat..."
demo_build "$dir"
demo_setup "$dir" "$hps"

# Shell-quoted, so a DIR with spaces still pastes and runs.
q="$(printf %q "$dir")"
operator="$q/bin/ulpnode serve --config $q/operator.yaml --log-format pretty"
shipper="$q/bin/ulpnode serve --config $q/shipper.yaml --log-format pretty"
chat="$q/bin/ulpchat --config $q/shipper.yaml"
book="$q/bin/ulpnode book --config $q/shipper.yaml --operator ocean-blue.example --request $q/booking.json"
disrupt="$q/bin/ulpctl disrupt --config $q/operator.yaml --booking OB-BKG-1042 --delay 72h --reason \"Engine repair, unscheduled call at Halifax.\""
ask="$q/bin/ulpnode ask --config $q/shipper.yaml --booking OB-BKG-1042 \"What caused the delay, and how firm is the new ETA?\""

# The browser UIs: on a Cloud Workstation, through its proxy.
ob_ui="http://ocean-blue.localhost:$OP_PORT/ui/"
cy_ui="http://cymbal-shoes.localhost:$SH_PORT/ui/"
if [[ -n "${WEB_HOST:-}" ]]; then
  ob_ui="https://$OP_PORT-$WEB_HOST/ui/"
  cy_ui="https://$SH_PORT-$WEB_HOST/ui/"
fi

if $tmux; then
  command -v tmux >/dev/null || { echo "hello-ulp: tmux is not installed; run without --tmux" >&2; exit 1; }
  session="${HELLO_ULP_SESSION:-hello-ulp}"
  tmux kill-session -t "$session" 2>/dev/null || true
  # A tmux server already running wouldn't see this shell's environment,
  # so pass on what the operator node needs.
  env_args=()
  [[ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]] && env_args+=(-e "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=$ANTHROPIC_API_KEY")
  # DESIGN's screen layout, panes addressed by ID: tmux renumbers panes by
  # position as they split, so indices would point at the wrong ones.
  #   Cymbal Shoes (you)     | Ocean Blue node log
  #   Cymbal Shoes node log  | Presenter (ulpctl)
  you=$(tmux new-session -d -s "$session" -x 200 -y 50 "${env_args[@]}" -P -F '#{pane_id}' bash)
  tmux set-option -t "$session" remain-on-exit on # a node that fails keeps its error on screen
  tmux set-option -t "$session" mouse on # click to switch panes, wheel to scroll (this session only)
  tmux set-option -t "$session" pane-border-status top
  ob_log=$(tmux split-window -h -t "$you" "${env_args[@]}" -P -F '#{pane_id}' "$operator")
  cy_log=$(tmux split-window -v -t "$you" -P -F '#{pane_id}' "$shipper")
  presenter=$(tmux split-window -v -t "$ob_log" -P -F '#{pane_id}' bash)
  tmux select-pane -t "$you" -T "Cymbal Shoes (you)"
  tmux select-pane -t "$ob_log" -T "Ocean Blue node (operator)"
  tmux select-pane -t "$cy_log" -T "Cymbal Shoes node (shipper)"
  tmux select-pane -t "$presenter" -T "Presenter (ulpctl)"
  sleep 1 # let the nodes start before the commands are typed
  tmux send-keys -t "$you" "$chat" Enter
  tmux send-keys -t "$presenter" "$disrupt"
  tmux select-pane -t "$you"
  echo "In tmux: the top-left pane is Cymbal's assistant (ulpchat). Ask it what"
  echo "ocean-blue.example can do, then to book (see the printout without --tmux for"
  echo "the sentences); answer y in the dialog. Once Cymbal's log (bottom left) shows"
  echo "the departure, press Enter in the bottom-right pane to disrupt, then ask the"
  echo "assistant: Ask ocean-blue.example why OB-BKG-1042 is delayed."
  echo "Browser UIs: $ob_ui (Sam) and $cy_ui (Alex)."
  [[ -n "${HELLO_ULP_NO_ATTACH:-}" ]] && exit 0 # tests
  exec tmux attach -t "$session"
fi

cat <<EOF

Hello ULP is set up in $dir. Open four terminals:

  Each company's browser UI, once its node runs (sign in as its persona):
       Ocean Blue:   $ob_ui   (Sam: bookings, Disrupt voyage…)
       Cymbal Shoes: $cy_ui   (Alex: the assistant; book and confirm there)

  1. Ocean Blue's node (the operator):
       $operator

  2. Cymbal Shoes' node (the shipper):
       $shipper

  3. Cymbal Shoes' assistant, the chat TUI (Ctrl-C quits):
       $chat

     Ask it about the carrier, then book: one message each (the fake
     model knows these; a real model takes any wording):
       We have a new carrier, ocean-blue.example. What can they do?
       Book one 40ft high-cube of sneakers for CY-PO-55120, Rotterdam to
       Newark, departing 2026-10-06, with ocean-blue.example. Consignee is
       Cymbal Footwear in Newark (cymbal-footwear.example). It has to arrive
       before Thursday the 15th.
     (The demo's dates are fixed, and CY-PO-55120 is the purchase order in
     Cymbal's private business file, so the delay summary below finds the
     receiving slot.)
     A dialog shows exactly what will be sent; answer y.

     Without the TUI, book from the command line instead (answer y):
       $book

     Ocean Blue confirms OB-BKG-1042 and starts the voyage at $hps simulated
     hour(s) per second. Watch Cymbal's log: each event arrives as a
     "← ulp.tnt.event … VERIFIED (kid …)  ALLOWED" line and a "· OB-BKG-1042
     …" line: gate-in, load, departure, estimated arrival...

  4. Once the vessel has departed, disrupt the voyage, as the presenter:
       $disrupt

     Cymbal's log shows the signed delay alert ("! alert recorded … high
     delay"), the ETA moving from the 13th to the 16th. Then Cymbal's own
     model says what that means for Cymbal: a "✦ summary … MISSES" line,
     since the vessel now arrives after Cymbal's receiving slot on the 15th
     (from its private business file, never sent).

  5. Ask Ocean Blue why, in the TUI:
       Ask ocean-blue.example why OB-BKG-1042 is delayed.
     or from the command line:
       $ask

     Ocean Blue's log shows the inquiry verified and allowed, and answered
     (a "✦ model" line; the fake model needs no API key), and the answer
     cites events and the alert that Cymbal holds signed.

Run it again from step 1 with a fresh booking by restarting both nodes
(they keep everything in memory).
EOF
